Left elbow pain.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Anna Rodriguez is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease. She presents today with left elbow pain.

The patient states she has been having pain in her left elbow. She sits at her desk for work and stays in the same motion all day. After work, it is hard for her to open and close her elbow. She reports swelling and stiffness in her left elbow.

She denies any numbness or tingling in her hands. She has a little bit of weakness in her arm, but nothing too significant. She denies any fever or chills.

Regarding her epilepsy, she states she has not had any recent seizures. She thinks her last seizure was a year ago. She is still taking Keppra. She is doing well with therapy. She has not seen any improvement in her depression, but she has been able to avoid medication since she is already taking Keppra. She denies any suicidal or homicidal thoughts.

Regarding her peptic ulcer disease, she reports doing well since her endoscopy. She has not had any issues since the procedure.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Constitutional: Denies fever or chills.
HENT: Endorses nasal congestion from allergies.
Neurological: Denies numbness or tingling.
Musculoskeletal: Endorses left elbow pain.

