MSK: Examination of the left elbow: Erythema and edema of the left elbow. Pain to palpation of the left olecranon. Warm to palpation. Pain with flexion and extension of the left elbow. Palpable left radial pulse.

RESULTS

X-ray of the left arm: No evidence of elbow fracture.

Endoscopy: Revealed gastritis.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Anna Rodriguez is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease. She presents today with left elbow pain.

Olecranon bursitis.
• Medical Reasoning: She is right-handed, but she is experiencing pain in her left elbow. She works at a desk all day, which may be causing repetitive trauma to her left elbow.
• Patient Education and Counseling: I advised her to rest her elbow and use ice. She will get a pillow for her elbow.
• Medical Treatment: Prescription for Meloxicam 15 mg once a day.

Epilepsy.
• Medical Reasoning: She has been doing well with therapy. She is currently taking Keppra 500 mg twice a day.
• Patient Education and Counseling: We discussed that she is doing well with her current treatment.
• Medical Treatment: Refill for Keppra 500 mg twice a day.

Depression.
• Medical Reasoning: She has been doing well with therapy.
• Patient Education and Counseling: We discussed that she is doing well with her current therapy. We also discussed medical treatment options.
• Medical Treatment: Prescription for Lexapro 10 mg once a day.

Peptic Ulcer Disease.
• Medical Reasoning: She had an endoscopy that revealed gastritis. She has been taking Protonix 40 mg once a day before meals.
• Patient Education and Counseling: We discussed that she is doing well since her endoscopy.
• Medical Treatment: Continue Protonix 40 mg once a day before meals.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up in 2 weeks. }}<|eot_id|>
