After reviewing the patient's pulmonary function test results and her current symptoms, I have recommended that we continue to use the Wixela as a daily treatment for her asthma. She is currently using it once a day, but we will try to reduce it to once a day. We will also add alvesco as a back-up inhaler. She will use it as needed. I will have her use the alvesco 80 mcg, 2 puffs twice daily. She will discontinue using her Wixela. We will repeat her PFT in 4 months.

The patient will continue to use her albuterol as needed. She will also continue to use her Zyrtec as needed.

The patient will continue to avoid peanuts and tree nuts. She will continue to carry an EpiPen.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up in 4 months for a repeat PFT.

