The patient states that she started noticing some unusual discharge last week. She notes that it smells different and is not the same color or consistency as usual. She states that she did not notice this at first because the right side of her vagina was hurting. She notes that the pain has not gone away.

The patient reports that she and her partner have been dating for three years. She states that she believes he started cheating on her about three months ago. The patient notes that she had an irregular Pap smear in the past, but she has not had one since. She states that her last Pap smear was about six months ago and was normal.

