Ears: Exam of the ears is unremarkable.
Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.
Cardiovascular: Heart is in regular rate and rhythm.

PHYSICAL EXAM

Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.
Cardiovascular: Heart is in regular rate and rhythm.
Musculoskeletal: Examination of the low back reveals tenderness to palpation in the right and middle low back. Pain with flexion and extension. No pain or numbness to palpation of the bilateral lower extremities.

RESULTS

None to date.

ASSESSMENT

1. Low back strain.
2. Diabetes.

PLAN

I have discussed the nature of the diagnosis and treatment options with the patient today. For his low back pain, I have recommended an x-ray of the lumbar spine. I also recommended physical therapy for strengthening and pain relief. I have prescribed Flexeril 5 mg to be taken once daily for muscle relaxation. I advised him to avoid strenuous activities after taking the medication. I also advised him to avoid driving after taking the medication.
For his diabetes, I recommended that he continue his current diet and exercise regimen. I advised him to continue taking his metformin twice daily. I also recommended that he monitor his blood glucose levels daily. I advised him to monitor his A1c regularly.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up in 1 week. }}<|eot_id|>
