The patient is an 82-year-old male with past medical history significant for hypertension and stage 3 chronic kidney disease. He presents for hospital follow-up after an acute on chronic CHF exacerbation. The patient reports that he was doing well until he began to notice that his ankles were swelling. He states that one day he got really short of breath and he even had to call 911. He reports that when the paramedics arrived, they placed him on a special mask to breathe. He states that when he got to the ER, his BP was "super high". The patient reports that he has been watching his diet, but he admits that he misses a dose of his medications at times.

The patient reports that he has been taking his medications for the most part, but he misses a dose or two. He denies chest pain.

The patient states that he is feeling better now and denies any shortness of breath or problems sleeping. He does state that he has a good afternoon nap. The patient denies any chest pain.

MEDICAL HISTORY

The patient reports a history of hypertension and stage 3 chronic kidney disease.

SURGICAL HISTORY

The patient reports a history of a renal artery stent placement.

SOCIAL HISTORY

